>

Everything has been explained what destroys the language. What has destoyed
it is the lack of up to date refgram after 2003 reforms.

What you are trying  is to destroy what is left.

Show me what you offer instead: the corpus of texts, the refgram, tutorials.

You show absolutely nothing.
At least write some texts in Lojban. Do something.

I can't see that.

and driving out speakers then ... wait that's what essentially every
> argument you put forth is founded on. You can wave your hands and talk
> about some unnamed people I've 'driven out' at the same time I point to the
> speakers I've brought to the language.
>
> "Please, change your attitude."
>
> My attitude is a direct response to being diminished and dismissed. I'll
> change it when that changes.
>

You've driven out not unnamed people. They had nicknames in IRC, in
Facebook.

Shall we drag this out of logs?
Should we? Of course I can do that. I'd just prefer doing other more
valuable work. But if this continues (which I hope will not) of course I'll
have to take some actions.

Why are you talking on behalf of other people that ti'e being dismissed?
Why Lojbab or me are not qualified and you are qualified?




